/** @page gitreleasenotes Release Notes

    @section gitv100 git Module Version 1.0.0

    <b>Build Requirements</b>
    - CMake 3.21 or newer is required for documentation configuration

    <b>Core Repository Operations</b>
    - dual-mode architecture: disk-backed and virtual/in-memory repositories
    - virtual filesystem API: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::readFile() "readFile()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::writeFile() "writeFile()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::deleteFile() "deleteFile()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::listFiles() "listFiles()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::fileExists() "fileExists()"
    - commit operations: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::commit() "commit()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::headCommitId() "headCommitId()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::lookupCommit() "lookupCommit()"
    - branch management: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::createBranch() "createBranch()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::deleteBranch() "deleteBranch()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::checkout() "checkout()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::branches() "branches()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::currentBranch() "currentBranch()"
    - tag operations: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::createTag() "createTag()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::deleteTag() "deleteTag()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::tags() "tags()"
    - diff and log: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::diff() "diff()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::diffPatch() "diffPatch()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::diffStats() "diffStats()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::log() "log()"
    - blame: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::blame() "blame()" with per-line commit attribution
    - stash (disk mode): @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::stash() "stash()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::stashPop() "stashPop()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::stashList() "stashList()"
    - remote operations: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::fetch() "fetch()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::push() "push()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::addRemote() "addRemote()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::removeRemote() "removeRemote()"
    - repository info: @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::status() "status()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::state() "state()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::configGet() "configGet()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::configSet() "configSet()"

    <b>Merge and Pull</b>
    - @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::merge() "merge()" with three conflict resolution strategies:
      detect-only, strategy-based (ours/theirs), and callback-based (for AI resolution)
    - @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::pull() "pull()" for fetch + merge in one operation
    - three-phase lock management for safe callback invocation during merge
    - typed hashdecls: @ref Qore::Git::GitMergeConflict, @ref Qore::Git::GitMergeResult

    <b>Convenience Factory</b>
    - @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::connectRemote() "connectRemote()" for creating virtual
      repositories connected to a remote with auto-fetch and checkout

    <b>Typed Hashdecls</b>
    - @ref Qore::Git::GitSignatureInfo, @ref Qore::Git::CommitInfo, @ref Qore::Git::DiffEntry,
      @ref Qore::Git::DiffStatsInfo, @ref Qore::Git::BlameHunkInfo, @ref Qore::Git::StashInfo

    <b>User Modules</b>
    - @ref gitdataproviderintro "GitDataProvider": data provider actions for read-file,
      write-file, list-files, commit, log, diff, and status
    - @ref gitconfigmanagerintro "GitConfigManager": high-level config management with
      sync/publish, environment branches, change proposals, and observer-based change detection
    - @ref gitforgehelperintro "GitForgeHelper": GitHub/GitLab PR/MR management
    - @ref gitconnectionsintro "GitConnections": connection provider for disk and virtual repos

    <b>Security and Robustness</b>
    - virtual repositories created with @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::createVirtual()
      "createVirtual()" are now genuinely in-memory (in-memory object database,
      reference database, config, and index) with <i>no</i> filesystem footprint;
      a disk-backed temporary repository is created transparently only if a remote
      is added (required for fetch/push pack negotiation)
    - temporary directories created for remote-backed virtual repositories honor
      @c TMPDIR, are created with mode 0700, and are tracked so they are reclaimed
      at module unload even if the owning object is leaked
    - file path arguments to @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::readFile() "readFile()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::writeFile() "writeFile()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::deleteFile() "deleteFile()", etc. are validated to
      reject absolute paths and \c ".." traversal outside the working tree; disk
      writes use @c O_NOFOLLOW so a symlink in the working tree cannot be used to
      overwrite an external file (throws \c GIT-PATH-ERROR)
    - remote URLs are validated; the \c "ext::" smart-transport scheme (arbitrary
      command execution) is rejected (throws \c GIT-REMOTE-ERROR)
    - @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::fetch() "fetch()" and
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::push() "push()" hold the repository lock for the
      duration of network I/O, preventing concurrent access to the underlying
      libgit2 repository from other threads
    - when a @ref Qore::SandboxManager "SandboxManager" is active,
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::fetch() "fetch()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::push() "push()",
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::pull() "pull()", and
      @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository::connectRemote() "connectRemote()" perform a
      best-effort network pre-flight: the remote host is resolved and every
      resolved address is validated against the network security policy
      (SSRF / private-network / cloud-metadata blocking) before connecting,
      throwing \c NETWORK-ACCESS-DENIED on a policy violation. This is
      advisory (libgit2 resolves/connects independently); coarse control
      remains enforced by the \c NETWORK functional domain
    - GitForgeHelper validates the GitLab instance URL (scheme, host, no embedded
      credentials; cleartext \c http requires an explicit \c allow_insecure
      option) before attaching the API token, and re-raises REST failures without
      credential-bearing request context
    - GitConnections rejects \c ".." path components in \c gitlocal:// URLs

    <b>GitDataProvider</b>
    - the \c log and \c diff action responses now use typed sub-types
      (\c GitCommitInfoDataType / \c GitSignatureInfoDataType /
      \c GitDiffEntryDataType) instead of untyped lists, so the UI exposes
      per-field mapping of commit and diff results
    - the \c diff and \c log actions preselect their options so the action
      form is populated rather than empty
*/
